Package: wmr-bridge
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: nightcinder <67344577+nightcinder@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10)
Recommends: bluez, network-manager
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/nightcinder/WMR_Bridge
Description: WMR motion controller host bridge over Wi-Fi
 The WMR Bridge daemon reads Motion Controller HID reports from BlueZ,
 decodes them, and serves the same FF11/FF12/FF14 payloads the ESP32
 firmware exposes over a WebSocket on Wi-Fi.
 .
 It runs as the wmr system user, needs read access to /dev/hidraw*, and
 requires a token for non-loopback listens.
